  "description": "Made from besan, a finely milled chickpea flour, chillas are thin, crepe-like pancakes that take just a few minutes to whip up.",
  "notes": "Make-ahead and storage: The batter can be made up to 1 day in advance. Mix well before using.\nChilla can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days.\nChilla can be frozen in an airtight container or zip-top bag for up to 1 month. To freeze, arrange chilla in a single layer on a parchment-lined baking sheet. When frozen, place into a resealable container or zip-top bag. Reheat in the microwave.",
